  "enhanced_information": "The clinical presentation of the 12-year-old girl, including cola-colored urine, mild facial puffiness, and a recent sore throat, suggests a diagnosis of post-infectious glomerulonephritis, likely following a streptococcal infection. The urinalysis findings of hematuria (indicated by RBC casts) and mild proteinuria support this diagnosis. In post-streptococcal glomerulonephritis, light microscopy typically reveals hypercellular and enlarged glomeruli due to an increase in glomerular cells in response to inflammation. This aligns with the consensus that hypercellularity is a hallmark of this condition. Therefore, the best description of the light microscopy findings in this case is 'hypercellular and enlarged glomeruli.'"
